  "notes": "Strict 1:1 with the portal pCO2 tool (modules/tools_tab/tools/pco2_tool.R). The portal has a single control flow: pco2_tool.R:207 loops for rep in c('A','B') unconditionally, calling calcCH4dry -> calcCO2 -> calcCH4/calcpCO2/calcpCO2P1/calcpCO2P2 (:224-260), then :280-297 takes calcMean/calcSd over the A/B pair for CO2_HS_Um, pCO2_HS_uatm, pCO2_HS_P1_uatm, pCO2_HS_P2_uatm, d13C_CO2 and CH4 (the CH4 pair is spelled CH4_umol_L_avg/_sd, :291-296). There is no single-value entry point in the portal, so the tool has no mode selector and no co2_aq_umol input: every case is the replicate chain.\n\nThe four measured columns are declared one param per replicate cell, named for the portal's own columns with the entry grid's _rep_ marker: lab_co2_co2ppm_rep_A/B, lab_co2_h2o_rep_A/B, lab_co2_ch4_rep_A/B and lab_co2_ico2_rep_A/B (pco2_tool.R:209-210 selects lab_co2_co2ppm/h2o/ch4 by their trailing letter, :283 reads lab_co2_ico2 for the d13C pair). The letter therefore travels in the field name. replicate_b_measured_alone_lands_on_b pins what that buys: a sample measured only in B yields the B keys and the B values, byte for byte those of full_chain_replicates, with the A keys absent and the _sd keys absent. Under a positional declaration that request could not be expressed, because the entry form drops a blank cell rather than sending a hole, so a lone B arrived as A and was computed and filed under the wrong letter.\n\nNo input is required. calcCO2 (calculation_functions.R:794-883) has no water-temperature term, so a row with no field temperature still yields the CH4-dry and headspace-CO2 columns; full_no_water_temp_still_yields_headspace_co2 pins that. The portal likewise computes with whatever the row holds and leaves the rest blank.\n\nLab temperature and lab pressure are the portal's two checkboxes (pco2_tool.R:28-29 for the UI, 194-204 for the mapping to 'cst'/'db'), modelled here as the explicit enums lab_temp_mode and lab_pressure_mode, both defaulting to 'db' because both checkboxes default to FALSE. The portal never passes calcCO2/calcCH4 the 'default' mode, so 'db' with a blank entry yields NA rather than falling back to the constant: full_lab_temp_db_missing_computes_nothing and full_lab_pressure_db_missing_computes_nothing pin that (only the two lab_co2_ch4_dry keys survive). calcCO2 converts a db lab pressure hPa->atm and uses lab_press_avg_atm as-is in cst mode; calcCH4 uses the 0.957237 atm literal in the formula and reads labPa only for its NA check, so the lab pressure mode moves CO2 but not CH4 (full_lab_pressure_cst leaves the CH4 keys equal to full_chain_replicates).\n\nField barometric pressure comes from the row's Field_BP with Field_BP_altitude as the fallback (pco2_tool.R:191 selects both into fieldData). calcCH4, calcpCO2P1 and calcpCO2P2 take Field_BP when it is present and within 700-1050 hPa and drop to Field_BP_altitude otherwise; both are declared inputs (pressure_hpa, pressure_altitude_hpa) so the fallback path is reachable. full_field_pressure_out_of_band_uses_altitude pins it; full_no_field_pressure_no_altitude pins that with neither pressure the P1/P2 and CH4 keys are absent while CO2_HS_Um and pCO2_HS_uatm still compute.\n\nThe portal applies no bound to lab_co2_lab_press; the 700-1050 hPa band exists only for field pressure, and there the portal falls back silently rather than failing. full_lab_pressure_above_1050_still_computes pins that a 1100 hPa lab pressure computes instead of raising.\n\nVolumes are constants only: calcCO2 reads vol_sa/vol_water from the constants table and the tool tab offers no control for them (its two editable tables are rawData at :104 and labCst at :119-124), so there are no vol_sa_ml/vol_water_ml request overrides. All cases use the constants-table values (vol_sa = vol_water = 0.03).\n\nThe portal's 'KEEP OLD' carry-forward (pco2_tool.R:301-315, which re-reads the stored row when calcMean/calcSd have nothing to average) is deliberately not emulated: these tools are stateless and have no stored row to fall back to. calcMean/calcSd return the character 'KEEP OLD' in that case and the wrapper omits the key, which is also how a portal tools-tab NA displays. full_single_replicate, replicate_b_measured_alone_lands_on_b, full_replicate_b_ch4_null and full_d13c_one_sided pin the omissions (a lone value still yields _avg; _sd is absent).\n\nfull_water_temp_at_reference_pco2_is_co2_over_0034 is the hand-checkable case: at 25 degC the van't Hoff exponential in calcpCO2 (calculation_functions.R:888-932) is 1, so pCO2_HS_uatm_{rep} is exactly CO2_HS_Um_{rep} / 0.034 (318.26554063262745 / 0.034 = 9360.751195077277).\n\nExpected values were derived from the portal formulas independently (a python transcription of calcCH4dry/calcCO2/calcCH4/calcpCO2/calcpCO2P1/calcpCO2P2/calcMean/calcSd) and then confirmed against the live OpenCPU runner at digits=17.\n\nOmission follows the portal exactly: a key is dropped when calcMean/calcSd return the 'KEEP OLD' sentinel (tested before coercion, since as.numeric('KEEP OLD') is NA) or when a prelude function returns as.numeric(NA) for a row it cannot compute. Nothing else is filtered. NaN and Inf are values the portal displays, so the wrapper emits them; they serialise to JSON null and the API drops nulls, so a case that produced one would list the key under absent with that reason. No case in this file reaches either."
}
